      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3891_Task4" name="CDP/Marketing syndicate consented audiences to activation channels…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: CDP/Marketing syndicate consented audiences to activation channels: email/SMS/push (links to VS-14/VS-75), ecommerce on-site personalization (links to VS-10), in-store/clienteling (links to VS-124/VS-63), and paid-media/publisher audiences (Meta/Google — links to VS-14.2) via consented audience export/hash-matching
Responsible (R): CDP / Marketing / IT
Accountable (A): CDP Lead
Duration: Per campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3891_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3891_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3891_Task5" name="CDP/Privacy enforce consent per channel (links to W3885), suppress…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: CDP/Privacy enforce consent per channel (links to W3885), suppress non-consented/invalid, and maintain the activation audit trail (who/what/channel/when) for NPC compliance (links to VS-91)
Responsible (R): CDP / Privacy / Marketing
Accountable (A): CDP Lead
Duration: Per activation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3891_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3891_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3891_Task6" name="CDP/Marketing track activation delivery and reach, reconcile to segment counts…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CDP/Marketing track activation delivery and reach, reconcile to segment counts, and capture downstream response for measurement (links to W3896)
Responsible (R): CDP / Marketing / Insights
Accountable (A): CDP Lead
Duration: Per campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3891_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3891_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
